{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory has a `card_spec.json` (oracle text/metadata) and a `card_impl.py` stub to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` (via grep) for rules. The implementation must follow the inherited `/workspace/PLAN.md`. \n   \n   Methodology constraints (verbatim intent):\n   - Strict TDD using the `tdd` skill: write ONE failing test through the engine's public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers), watch it fail (red), write minimal code (green), repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - Test the real engine, not a stand-in. Drive cards the way a player would, through test_utils.\n   - Reuse before you add; mirror the nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal and shared.\n   - Requirements are source of truth — re-check oracle clauses against card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt.\n   - **Guard the engine: after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression.**\n   - **Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/` (grader uses authoritative copies). Do NOT modify or add FDN `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`.**\n   - **Additive-only engine modifications**: may add methods/classes/helpers/files inside engine/ and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Card class names in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` must not change. SOS tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, max 30 per card.\n   - Final user message: respond TEXT ONLY (this summary), no tool calls.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Converge, Affinity (self + granted), cost reduction, Casualty, Miracle, Paradigm, Prepared, Surveil, planeswalker loyalty abilities, skip-turns, land animation, spell copying, counter spells, graveyard→exile replacement.\n   - Engine architecture: GameObject/CardImpl hierarchy; hooks (can_cast, cost_reduction(game)->int, on_cast, on_resolve via self.chosen_targets, get_targets, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_modes, Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities, Land.get_mana_abilities).\n   - Trigger system (TriggerManager.register/fire_event, TriggerRegistration with event_type/condition/effect/source/controller; APNAP ordering; subclass event matching).\n   - Replacement effects (ReplacementEffect, ReplacementManager.apply; MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent has destination/prevented/card).\n   - Continuous effects 7-layer system (Layer.TYPE=4, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7 with SubLayer.SET_PT=7b/MODIFY_PT=7c; DURATION_PERMANENT=-1/DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0; EffectManager.apply_all resets via _reset_characteristics each cycle).\n   - Casting pipeline: cast_spell stores `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (distinct Color enums, excludes colorless); cast_spell_free for free casts; copy_spell shallow-copies and pushes without going through cast_spell.\n   - ManaCost.parse(), ManaCost.cmc; ManaPool.last_payment_colors (distinct non-colorless Colors, auto-pay generic prefers colorless then colored in enum order).\n   - DeterministicPlayer scripted choices (FIFO deque); test_utils cast_spell scripts targets via player._script.appendleft.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — The authoritative plan. Contains engine gaps G1-G8 and per-card plans. Critical details:\n     - G1 (DONE): fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in cast_spell + cast_spell_free → unblocks sos_226, sos_257.\n     - G2 (DONE): BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent → sos_57, sos_120.\n     - G3 (TODO): GameState.skip_turns dict + advance_phase logic → sos_97.\n     - G4 (DONE): reset cards_drawn_this_turn in _do_untap_step → sos_201.\n     - G5 (TODO): surveil(game, player, n) helper in game.py → sos_97.\n     - G6 (TODO): cast_spell_alt_cost(game, player, card, from_zone, alt_cost) in casting.py → sos_201.\n     - G7 (TODO): in get_cost_reduction, aggregate controller permanents' grants_cost_reduction(game, card) → sos_245.\n     - G8: land animation — no new engine, reuse layers + override _reset_characteristics → sos_257.\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — MODIFIED (G1). Added after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` in BOTH cast_spell (step 9) and cast_spell_free:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n         game,\n         SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, player=player, card=card, controller=player),\n     )\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — MODIFIED (G2). Added after BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         player: Any = None\n         is_precombat: bool = True\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — MODIFIED (G2 + G4). In _do_untap_step added `active.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` after land_plays reset. In run_turn added elif branches firing BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent for (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None) with is_precombat=True and (POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None) with is_precombat=False.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` — CREATED (last action). Tests for TogetherAsOne: properties (Sorcery, name, mana_cost {6}), Converge behavior (2 colors → gain 2 life / deal 2 to player / target player draws 2; all colorless → X=0; 3 colors → 3 damage to creature; 1 color → X=1). Uses helper `_stock_library` to add Creature filler cards to library for draw tests, casts via cast_spell with targets=[player, target].\n   - Card stubs all follow pattern: `class <Name>(CardImpl): pass` — must change base class but keep class name. Class names: TheDawningArchaic(sos_1), TogetherAsOne(sos_4), EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(sos_13), ManaSculpt(sos_57), RalZarekGuestLecturer(sos_97), ImprovisationCapstone(sos_120), LoreholdTheHistorian(sos_201), SilverquillTheDisputant(sos_226), WitherbloomTheBalancer(sos_245), GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(sos_257).\n   - FDN reference impls read (analogues): fdn_205 (WardensOfTheCycle, converge/colors_spent), fdn_6 (ClawsOut, cost_reduction affinity-style), fdn_167 (TolarianTerror, cost_reduction counting GY instant/sorcery), fdn_194 (EtaliPrimalStorm, AttacksTriggeredEvent + cast_spell_free loop with choose_yes_no), fdn_244 (Progenitus, MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent + _reset_characteristics override), fdn_48 (Refute, counter via _counter_spell removing from game.stack._items, can_cast/get_targets stack-target pattern, _get_chosen_target helper), fdn_248 (ThousandYearStorm, SpellCastTriggeredEvent + copy_spell + new-target choosing), fdn_245 (RubyDaringTracker, ManaAbility list + AttacksTriggeredEvent buff), fdn_44 (KaitoCunningInfiltrator, Planeswalker get_loyalty_abilities returning LoyaltyAbility list, effects read pw._resolve_target).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - None encountered yet. Baseline engine tests passed (1145) before and after G1/G2/G4 changes.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Verified G1/G2/G4 additive engine changes do not regress the engine suite (1145 passed both times). Confirmed firing SpellCastTriggeredEvent is safe because the FDN cards relying on it (fdn_248, fdn_44) have no engine tests, and copy_spell bypasses cast_spell (so copies won't re-trigger casualty/storm). Determined Converge X = len(card.colors_spent) since last_payment_colors already returns distinct non-colorless Colors.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System/task prompt) \"Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD)... Read PLAN.md in full... strict TDD... Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in /workspace/cards/sos/. Each card directory contains a card_spec.json... Use completed FDN cards... Refer to RULEBOOK.txt... You are expected to make changes to the engine... Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/...\"\n   - (system-reminders about deferred tools and available skills)\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - sos_4 (in progress): implement TogetherAsOne (Converge). Test file written; need to run/red, then implement.\n   - sos_245 Witherbloom: add engine G7, implement cost_reduction (creatures you control) + grants_cost_reduction for your instants/sorceries; Flying|Deathtouch; 5/5.\n   - sos_1 The Dawning Archaic: 7/7 Reach, cost_reduction per instant/sorcery in GY, AttacksTriggeredEvent free-cast from GY + scoped MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent redirect to exile.\n   - sos_57 Mana Sculpt: copy Refute counter pattern; if control Wizard, register delayed BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (G2) trigger adding {C} = mana spent.\n   - sos_226 Silverquill: 4/4 Flying|Vigilance; SpellCastTriggeredEvent (G1) casualty 1 — sac creature power>=1 → copy_spell.\n   - sos_257 Great Hall: Land mana abilities + {5} animation (Layer.TYPE + SET_PT, override _reset_characteristics) + SpellCastTriggeredEvent buff.\n   - sos_97 Ral Zarek: Planeswalker loyalty 3; +1 surveil 2 (G5); -1 players discard; -2 reanimate MV<=3; -7 five coins → skip_turns (G3).\n   - sos_201 Lorehold: 5/5 Flying|Haste; miracle {2} via DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + cast_spell_alt_cost (G6); opponent-upkeep loot.\n   - sos_13 Emeritus of Truce: 3/3 ETB Inkling token + become prepared; activated copy of STP back-half.\n   - sos_120 Improvisation Capstone: Sorcery Lesson; exile-until-MV>=4 free-cast (Etali loop); Paradigm recurring recast from exile each first main phase (G2).\n   - Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each card; engine must stay at 1145 passing (plus new SOS tests passing).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Implementing sos_4 (Together as One, Converge) — task #2 marked in_progress. I just wrote `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` (7 behavior + 3 property tests). The card is currently still a stub: `class TogetherAsOne(CardImpl): pass`. The planned implementation: change base to `Sorcery`, set name/mana_cost {6}; `on_resolve` computes `X = len(getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", []) or [])`, reads `self.chosen_targets` ([0]=target player to draw X via draw_card, [1]=any target for X damage via deal_damage), and `self.controller.life += X`; `get_targets` returns two TargetRequirements (target player; any target = player or CREATURE) with filter_fns capturing game.players. The test file uses `cast_spell(game, 0, \"Together as One\", targets=[player, target])` and stocks library with filler creatures for draw tests.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run the sos_4 tests to confirm they fail (red): `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py -q`, then implement `TogetherAsOne` in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` as a `Sorcery` with the Converge `on_resolve`/`get_targets` described above, re-run sos_4 tests (green), then run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` to guard the engine. This directly continues the in-progress task #2 (sos_4), which is next in the PLAN.md implementation order (step 2: \"sos_4 (Converge — pure on_resolve, no new engine)\").\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/a8998a71-cb9f-462b-a621-0c4f4edc8cf2.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent