{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory has a `card_spec.json` (oracle text/metadata) and a `card_impl.py` stub to fill in. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt`. Follow the inherited `/workspace/PLAN.md`.\n   \n   Methodology constraints (verbatim intent):\n   - Strict TDD using the `tdd` skill: write ONE failing test through the engine's public interface (test_utils: create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers), watch it fail (red), write minimal code (green), repeat. Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - Test the real engine, not a stand-in. Drive cards the way a player would, through test_utils.\n   - Reuse before you add; mirror the nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal and shared.\n   - Requirements are source of truth — re-check oracle clauses against card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt.\n   - **Guard the engine: after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression.**\n   - **Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/` (grader uses authoritative copies). Do NOT modify or add FDN `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`.**\n   - **Additive-only engine modifications**: may add methods/classes/helpers/files inside engine/ and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Card class names in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` must not change. SOS tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, max 30 per card.\n   - Most recent user message: respond TEXT ONLY (this summary), no tool calls.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Converge, Affinity (self + granted), cost reduction, Casualty, counter spells, delayed triggers, Miracle, Paradigm, Prepared, Surveil, planeswalker loyalty, skip-turns, land animation, spell copying, graveyard→exile redirection.\n   - Engine hooks: cost_reduction(game)->int, grants_cost_reduction(game, card)->int (NEW G7), on_resolve (via self.chosen_targets), get_targets (returns list[TargetRequirement]), can_cast, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_mana_abilities, _reset_characteristics.\n   - Trigger system: TriggerManager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)); fire_event pushes matching trigger StackObjects (APNAP order); unregister(source) by identity. Subclass event matching via isinstance.\n   - Events: SpellCastTriggeredEvent (spell/player/card/controller), BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (player/is_precombat), AttacksTriggeredEvent (creature/attacker), MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent (destination/prevented/card).\n   - Continuous effects 7-layer system: Layer.TYPE=4, Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7 (SubLayer.SET_PT=7b, MODIFY_PT=7c), DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. EffectManager.apply_all calls _reset_objects (which calls each battlefield object's _reset_characteristics) then applies sorted effects.\n   - Casting: cast_spell stores `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (distinct non-colorless Colors). cast_spell_free for free casts from any zone. copy_spell shallow-copies and pushes (bypasses cast_spell). ManaCost.cmc = generic + sum(pips.values()) + len(hybrid). ManaPool.add(mana_type, amount).\n   - test_utils.cast_spell has UNCONDITIONAL empty-stack check (line 277) — counters must use engine.casting.cast_spell directly. DeterministicPlayer pops all choices (choose, choose_target, choose_yes_no, choose_card, choose) from one FIFO `_script` deque. test_utils._resolve_top_of_stack pops+resolves stack until empty.\n   - Combat: declare_attackers_step does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent (engine gap); test_utils.declare_attackers doesn't resolve stack. Attack triggers tested by manual register_triggers + fire_event + _resolve_top_of_stack.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — MODIFIED (G1 prior, G7 + exile-on-resolution this session).\n     - G7 in get_cost_reduction (after computing `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`):\n       ```python\n       granted = 0\n       battlefield = game.get_battlefield(controller)\n       if battlefield is not None:\n           for perm in battlefield.get_all():\n               grant_hook = getattr(perm, \"grants_cost_reduction\", None)\n               if callable(grant_hook):\n                   granted += grant_hook(game, card)\n       generic = card.mana_cost.generic if card.mana_cost else 0\n       return max(0, min(raw + granted, generic))\n       ```\n     - exile-on-resolution seam in _resolve_spell (instant/sorcery else branch):\n       ```python\n       dest = Zone.GRAVEYARD\n       if getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolution\", False):\n           dest = Zone.EXILE\n       move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)\n       ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` + tests.py — DONE (9 tests). TogetherAsOne(Sorcery), {6}, get_targets [target player, any target], on_resolve: X=len(colors_spent), draw X to chosen_targets[0], deal X to chosen_targets[1], controller.life += X.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` + tests.py — DONE (11 tests). WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature), {6}{B}{G}, subtypes {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, LEGENDARY, Flying|Deathtouch, 5/5. cost_reduction = _count_creatures(controller); grants_cost_reduction = (if card is INSTANT/SORCERY) _count_creatures(controller).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` + tests.py — DONE (12 tests). TheDawningArchaic(Creature), {10}, subtypes {\"Avatar\"}, LEGENDARY, REACH, 7/7. cost_reduction = count instant/sorcery in GY. register_triggers: AttacksTriggeredEvent, condition event.creature is self, effect: may cast target instant/sorcery from GY free (set target._exile_on_resolution=True, cast_spell_free from Zone.GRAVEYARD).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` + tests.py — DONE (8 tests). ManaSculpt(Instant), {1}{U}{U}. Helpers _get_chosen_target, _counter_spell (removes from game.stack._items + controller STACK zone + add to owner GY), _controls_wizard. on_resolve: capture amount=target.source.mana_cost.cmc, counter, if amount>0 and Wizard: _register_delayed_mana (TriggerRegistration on BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent, condition event.player is controller, effect: add {C}×amount + unregister(self)).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` + tests.py — DONE (9 tests). SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature), {2}{W}{B}, {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, LEGENDARY, Flying|Vigilance, 4/4. register_triggers: SpellCastTriggeredEvent, condition caster is controller + instant/sorcery (stores self._casualty_spell), effect: find creatures power>=1, choose_yes_no, choose victim, sacrifice, find original StackObject in game.stack._items, copy_spell + push. Has static _choose_new_targets helper (returns None if no targets).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` — STILL STUB. `class GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(CardImpl): pass`. card_spec: Land, \"{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\" It's still a land.\"\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — Land class (line 480): can_cast returns False; get_mana_abilities returns []. ActivatedAbility (cost, effect, description), ManaAbility (cost, mana_produced, description), LoyaltyAbility. Creature.power = modified_power + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters. CardImpl._reset_characteristics resets card_types and keywords only.\n   - `/workspace/engine/abilities.py` — line 212: `cost_paid = ability.cost(game, ability.source)`; activate_ability dispatches ActivatedAbilityInstance/LoyaltyAbilityInstance.\n   - `/workspace/engine/basic_lands.py` — ManaAbility pattern reference for \"{T}: Add {mana}\".\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_245/card_impl.py` — RubyDaringTracker: get_mana_abilities returns ManaAbility list with _tap_cost (checks/taps source); AttacksTriggeredEvent buff via ContinuousEffect MODIFY_PT.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - sos_4 test_target_player_draws_x failed (asserted +2 got +1): the spell card itself leaves player 0's hand when cast, confounding the before/after hand count. Fixed by making the draw target player 1 (opponent) and stocking/measuring player 1's library/hand instead.\n   - No engine regressions encountered; 1145 passing maintained after every change.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed combat never fires AttacksTriggeredEvent and test_utils doesn't resolve post-declare; adopted the fdn_244 pattern of driving managers directly (register_triggers + fire_event + _resolve_top_of_stack) for attack-trigger tests rather than modifying combat (to avoid regression risk).\n   - Found _resolve_spell moves instant/sorcery stack→graveyard without replacement consultation; added minimal additive flag seam `_exile_on_resolution`.\n   - Found test_utils.cast_spell rejects non-empty stack; used engine.casting.cast_spell directly for counter scenarios (sos_57).\n   - Used ManaCost.cmc as proxy for \"amount of mana spent\" (engine doesn't track total mana paid, only colors).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Initial continuation system prompt with full prior summary) describing the SOS implementation task.\n   - Multiple identical system-reminders: \"Called the Read tool...\" / \"Result of calling the Read tool...\" providing tests.py for sos_4, turn.py, events.py, plus notes that casting.py and PLAN.md were read before compaction, plus deferred-tools list.\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch for TaskUpdate).\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\" (this summary request).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - sos_257 Great Hall (IN PROGRESS): Land with {T}: Add {C}; {T},Pay 1 life: Add any color (instant/sorcery restriction simplified); {5}: animate to 2/4 Wizard creature (still a land) with cast-trigger +1/+0 EOT buff.\n   - sos_97 Ral Zarek (Planeswalker): G3 skip_turns dict + advance_phase logic; G5 surveil helper; loyalty 3; +1 surveil 2; -1 players discard; -2 reanimate MV<=3; -7 five coins → skip_turns.\n   - sos_201 Lorehold: 5/5 Flying|Haste; Miracle {2} via DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + G6 cast_spell_alt_cost; opponent-upkeep loot.\n   - sos_13 Emeritus of Truce: 3/3 ETB Inkling token + become Prepared; activated copy of STP back-half.\n   - sos_120 Improvisation Capstone: Sorcery Lesson; exile-until-MV>=4 free-cast (Etali loop); Paradigm recurring recast from exile each first main phase (G2).\n   - After each card: `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` must stay at 1145 + new SOS tests passing.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Implementing sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex (task #7, in_progress). No card_impl or tests written yet. Studied the Land class, ManaAbility/ActivatedAbility, continuous_effects.py (7-layer system), and _reset_characteristics. Determined the animation plan (G8 — no new engine; reuse layers + override _reset_characteristics): GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land) with base_power=0/base_toughness=0/modified_power/modified_toughness/counters/damage_marked/summoning_sick/is_attacking/is_blocking attributes and a power/toughness property; {5} ActivatedAbility (cost pays {5} generic) that, if not already a creature, sets self._animated=True and registers permanent ContinuousEffects (Layer.TYPE adding CREATURE + \"Wizard\" subtype; SET_PT setting modified P/T to 2/4); override _reset_characteristics to reset modified_power/toughness to base and subtypes to original each cycle; register_triggers wires SpellCastTriggeredEvent (condition: controller casts instant/sorcery AND self._animated) adding a DURATION_END_OF_TURN MODIFY_PT +1/+0 effect; get_mana_abilities returns two ManaAbilities ({T}: Add {C}; {T}+pay 1 life: add chosen color). The last action was a Grep confirming ability cost invocation signature `ability.cost(game, ability.source)` (abilities.py:212).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue sos_257: first read `/workspace/engine/abilities.py` (around line 158-220) to confirm exactly how ActivatedAbility cost/effect callables are invoked and how {5} generic mana payment should be implemented in the cost callable, plus check basic_lands.py for the canonical \"{T}: Add {C}\" ManaAbility pattern and how `get_activated_abilities` is wired to a generic-mana cost. Then write the sos_257 tests.py (properties first: Land, name \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\", {T} mana abilities), confirm red, and implement GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex incrementally (mana abilities → {5} animation → cast-trigger buff), running `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py -q` then `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` (must stay 1145). This directly continues task #7 which is in_progress per the PLAN.md implementation order.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/a8998a71-cb9f-462b-a621-0c4f4edc8cf2.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8998a71-cb9f-462b-a621-0c4f4edc8cf2","uuid":"a191c300-4843-42c9-8d51-4dcfeeb5b34a","timestamp":