{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HnVM57tVxEHjoeZLsgn6xg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN.md — SOS card implementations (1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257)\n2\t\n3\tThis is the hand-off from the planning phase. The implementation agent inherits\n4\tONLY this file. Everything needed to implement the 10 cards and the supporting\n5\tengine changes is below: exact files, hooks, events, FDN analogues, and edge\n6\tcases. Hard rules from `AGENTS.md` still apply (additive-only engine changes —\n7\tnever rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; class names in\n8\t`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` must not change; write SOS tests at\n9\t`cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, max 30 per card; do not touch `engine_tests/` or\n10\tFDN `tests.py`).\n11\t\n12\tVerified engine facts this plan relies on:\n13\t- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` pipeline pushes a `StackObject` (step 8) but\n14\t  **never fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`** (no `fire_event` call exists in\n15\t  casting.py). `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` is the free-cast\n16\t  path. `cast_spell` stores `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`.\n17\t- `engine/card.py`: hooks are `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`,\n18\t  `on_resolve` (targets via `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets`,\n19\t  `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`,\n20\t  `get_modes`; `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities()`, `Land.get_mana_abilities()`.\n21\t  `Creature.power/toughness` are computed properties; `modified_power/modified_toughness`\n22\t  are the layer-7c write targets; `_reset_characteristics()` resets them each\n23\t  `EffectManager.apply_all()` cycle. `ManaCost.cmc` gives mana value.\n24\t- `engine/events.py`: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)`,\n25\t  `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()`\n26\t  (fires for BOTH players' upkeeps — condition must check `game.active_player`),\n27\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)`, `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`\n28\t  (has `destination`, `prevented`, `card`).\n29\t- `engine/game.py`: `draw_card` fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and increments\n30\t  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` (**but this counter is never reset** — gap #4).\n31\t  Helpers: `deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card, discard,\n32\t  create_token, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap`.\n33\t- `engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` at upkeep;\n34\t  `_do_untap_step` resets `land_plays_remaining`; **no main-phase event is fired**\n35\t  (gap #2). `_do_cleanup_step` calls `effect_manager.remove_expired` (sweeps\n36\t  `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`).\n37\t- `engine/game_state.py`: `extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO popped in `advance_phase`;\n38\t  `_normal_next_index` tracks normal rotation. **No skip-turn mechanism** (gap #3).\n39\t- `engine/combat.py::declare_attackers_step` (line ~228) gates attacker candidates\n40\t  on `hasattr(c, \"base_power\") and _can_attack(c)`; `_can_attack` checks\n41\t  `summoning_sick` vs `HASTE`. Combat damage reads `getattr(creature, \"power\"/\"toughness\")`\n42\t  and `damage_marked`. **An animated land must expose these attributes** (relevant to gap #8).\n43\t- `engine/abilities.py`: `activate_ability` handles loyalty abilities\n44\t  (sorcery-speed + once-per-turn enforced) but **does not plumb targets** — loyalty\n45\t  effects read targets off the source (e.g. `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)`,\n46\t  as fdn_44 does). Tests set the attribute before activating.\n47\t- `engine/stack.py::copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)`\n48\t  shallow-copies the source card, pushes a copy that resolves without zone moves.\n49\t- `engine/continuous_effects.py`: `Layer.TYPE` (4), `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` (7)\n50\t  with `SubLayer.SET_PT` (7b) / `MODIFY_PT` (7c); `DURATION_PERMANENT` / `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`.\n51\t- `engine/types.py::Keyword` has FLYING, HASTE, REACH, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, etc.\n52\t  (no AFFINITY/CONVERGE/CASUALTY/MIRACLE/SURVEIL/PREPARED/PARADIGM — those are\n53\t  hook-driven, NOT keyword flags). `ManaType` includes COLORLESS.\n54\t\n55\t---\n56\t\n57\t## 1. Engine gaps\n58\t\n59\tPrefer the shared seams: firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (one change, four cards)\n60\tand a new beginning-of-main-phase event (one change, two cards) carry most of the\n61\tweight. Everything below is additive.\n62\t\n63\t| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n64\t|---|---|---|---|\n65\t| **G1. \"Whenever you cast a spell\" triggers actually fire** | After pushing the `StackObject` in BOTH `cast_spell` (step 8) and `cast_spell_free` (step 5), call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`. Import the event. | `engine/casting.py` | sos_226 (casualty), sos_257 (Wizard buff); also un-breaks fdn_248/fdn_44 |\n66\t| **G2. \"At the beginning of your next/each main phase\" trigger** | Add `@dataclass class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent): player: Any = None`. In `run_turn`, when `game.phase in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN)` and `game.step is None`, fire it with `player=game.active_player` BEFORE `priority_loop`. | `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py` | sos_57 (delayed mana), sos_120 (paradigm recast) |\n67\t| **G3. Skip-turns** | Add `self.skip_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` to `GameState.__init__`. In `advance_phase`, after computing the would-be next `active_player_index` (from `extra_turns` or `_normal_next_index`), while `skip_turns.get(idx, 0) > 0`: decrement it, leave `_normal_next_index` pointing at that seat (so they're still \"next\" later), and set the turn to the other seat. Guard against both players skipping (infinite loop) → if all candidates are skipped, just proceed. | `engine/game_state.py` | sos_97 (−7 ultimate) |\n68\t| **G4. Reset first-draw tracking each turn** | In `_do_untap_step`, set `game.active_player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0`. (Counter exists in `draw_card` but is never reset, so \"first card drawn this turn\" is unreliable.) | `engine/turn.py` | sos_201 (miracle) |\n69\t| **G5. Surveil N** | New helper `surveil(game, player, n)` in `engine/game.py`: take top `n` of library; for each, ask `player.choose(\"graveyard\"/\"top\", ...)` (DeterministicPlayer scripts the answer); move chosen to graveyard via `move_to_zone`, leave rest on top. | `engine/game.py` | sos_97 (+1) |\n70\t| **G6. Cast for an alternative cost (miracle {2})** | New helper `cast_spell_alt_cost(game, player, card, from_zone, alt_cost: ManaCost)` in `engine/casting.py`: same body as `cast_spell` but pay `alt_cost` instead of `card.mana_cost` (still run targets/`on_cast`/push/fire G1). Reuse by extracting or copying the targeting+push block. | `engine/casting.py` | sos_201 (miracle); reusable by any alt-cost card |\n71\t| **G7. Static cost-reduction granted to OTHER spells (affinity granting)** | In `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, also add reductions contributed by the controller's permanents: `for perm in game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all(): fn = getattr(perm, \"grants_cost_reduction\", None); if callable(fn): raw += fn(game, card)`. Keep the existing `max(0, min(raw, generic))` clamp. | `engine/casting.py` | sos_245 (grants affinity to your instants/sorceries) |\n72\t| **G8. Land becomes a creature (animation)** | No new shared engine class needed — reuse `Layer.TYPE` + `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`/`SET_PT` continuous effects. The card itself must (a) carry the creature-combat attributes combat.py reads (`base_power`, `modified_power/toughness`, `damage_marked`, `is_attacking`, `is_blocking`, `summoning_sick`, `plus_one_counters`, `minus_one_counters`) and a computed/plain `power`/`toughness`, and (b) override `_reset_characteristics` so animation re-applies each `apply_all` cycle. See sos_257 below. Only flag here: combat.py line ~228 requires `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")` for a thing to be an attacker. | `engine/continuous_effects.py` (already sufficient) | sos_257 |\n73\t\n74\tNote on loyalty targeting (sos_97): no engine change — follow the fdn_44\n75\tconvention where the loyalty `effect` reads its target from an attribute on the\n76\tplaneswalker (e.g. `pw._resolve_target` / a list you set), and tests set that\n77\tattribute before calling `activate_ability`.\n78\t\n79\t---\n80\t\n81\t## 2. Per-card plan\n82\t\n83\tEach card's class is already stubbed at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` extending\n84\t`CardImpl` with `pass`; change the base class to the right type but keep the class\n85\tname. Set `name`, `mana_cost = ManaCost.parse(...)`, types/subtypes/supertypes,\n86\t`keywords`, and (creatures) `base_power/base_toughness` in `__init__` like the FDN\n87\texamples.\n88\t\n89\t### sos_4 — Together as One (`TogetherAsOne`, Sorcery) — Converge\n90\t- **Clauses:** \"Converge — Target player draws X, deals X damage to any target,\n91\t  you gain X life, where X = number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n92\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (Wardens of the Cycle) — reads colors spent.\n93\t- **Seam:** `cast_spell` already sets `card.colors_spent` (list of `ManaType`\n94\t  spent). In `on_resolve`, `X = len({c for c in self.colors_spent if c != ManaType.COLORLESS})`.\n95\t  Two targets via `get_targets`: (1) target player (draw), (2) \"any target\"\n96\t  (creature or player) for damage. Use `draw_card`, `deal_damage`, and add life.\n97\t- **New engine:** none.\n98\t- **Edge cases:** X=0 when only generic/colorless mana paid; target player for\n99\t  draw may differ from damage target; damage target may be a player or creature;\n100\t  reading `self.colors_spent` requires the spell to have been cast via `cast_spell`\n101\t  (tests using `cast_spell` helper get this; if a test sets the board directly,\n102\t  set `card.colors_spent` manually). Generic mana payment picks which colors are\n103\t  spent — tests should stock the mana pool with the exact colors they want counted.\n104\t\n105\t### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer (`WitherbloomTheBalancer`, Creature 5/5) — Affinity (self + granted)\n106\t- **Clauses:** \"Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control).\"\n107\t  / \"Flying, deathtouch.\" / \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n108\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (Claws Out) — `cost_reduction` counting subtype.\n109\t- **Seam:** Self-affinity → `cost_reduction(self, game)` returns number of\n110\t  creatures `self.controller` controls (count battlefield objects with\n111\t  `CardType.CREATURE`; the spell isn't on the battlefield yet so it won't count\n112\t  itself). Keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`. Granting affinity to\n113\t  your instants/sorceries → implement `grants_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)`\n114\t  returning `(# creatures you control)` when `spell`'s types include INSTANT/SORCERY\n115\t  and `spell.controller is self.controller`, else 0 — consumed by **G7**.\n116\t- **New engine:** G7.\n117\t- **Edge cases:** only reduces generic (engine clamps); granted reduction must NOT\n118\t  apply to opponents' spells or to non-instants/sorceries; granted reduction stacks\n119\t  with the spell's own `cost_reduction` (e.g. a card that also has self-affinity);\n120\t  Witherbloom must be on the battlefield for the grant to apply (it iterates the\n121\t  battlefield).\n122\t\n123\t### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic (`TheDawningArchaic`, Creature 7/7) — cost reduction + attack recast + exile replacement\n124\t- **Clauses:** \"Costs {1} less for each instant/sorcery in your graveyard.\" /\n125\t  \"Reach\" / \"Whenever it attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery from your\n126\t  graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your\n127\t  graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n128\t- **Analogues:** `cards/fdn/fdn_167` (Tolarian Terror) for `cost_reduction`;\n129\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali) for attack-trigger + `cast_spell_free`;\n130\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_244` (Progenitus) for the graveyard→exile replacement.\n131\t- **Seam:** `keywords = Keyword.REACH`. `cost_reduction` counts INSTANT/SORCERY in\n132\t  `self.controller`'s graveyard (copy fdn_167). `register_triggers`: on\n133\t  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` where `event.creature is self`, pick a target\n134\t  instant/sorcery in your graveyard (offer via `choose_yes_no` like Etali, choose\n135\t  the card), then **register a one-shot `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`\n136\t  replacement scoped to that card** (condition `event.card is the_spell`;\n137\t  replacement moves it to exile and sets `event.prevented = True`, like Progenitus\n138\t  but destination = exile), then `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, the_spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n139\t- **New engine:** none (reuses existing replacement + free-cast seams).\n140\t- **Edge cases:** no instant/sorcery in graveyard → trigger does nothing; the\n141\t  exile-instead replacement must fire when the cast copy resolves and `_resolve_spell`\n142\t  tries to move it to graveyard; unregister/scope the replacement so it doesn't\n143\t  affect other cards (condition on identity); Reach is only relevant to blocking\n144\t  (already handled by the engine's flying/reach interaction).\n145\t\n146\t### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt (`ManaSculpt`, Instant) — counter + delayed mana\n147\t- **Clauses:** \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to\n148\t  the mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n149\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) for the counter (can_cast checks stack\n150\t  non-empty; get_targets returns stack-object target; `_counter_spell` removes from\n151\t  `game.stack._items` and moves card to graveyard).\n152\t- **Seam:** Copy Refute's `can_cast`/`get_targets`/`_counter_spell`. On resolve:\n153\t  compute `mana_spent = len(target_stack_obj.source.colors_spent)` (or the spell's\n154\t  cmc if `colors_spent` is unavailable — prefer `colors_spent` since that's the\n155\t  literal \"mana spent\"). If `self.controller` controls a creature with subtype\n156\t  \"Wizard\", register a **delayed trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n157\t  (G2)** whose condition fires once for `event.player is self.controller`, adds\n158\t  `mana_spent` `{C}` to the controller's mana pool, then self-unregisters.\n159\t- **New engine:** G2.\n160\t- **Edge cases:** countering fizzles if target left the stack; no Wizard → no\n161\t  delayed mana; \"next main phase\" = the controller's next precombat OR postcombat\n162\t  main, whichever comes first (the one-shot fires on the first matching event then\n163\t  removes itself); record the mana amount at resolution (target is gone by then).\n164\t\n165\t### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant (`SilverquillTheDisputant`, Creature 4/4) — grants Casualty 1\n166\t- **Clauses:** \"Flying, vigilance.\" / \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has\n167\t  casualty 1 (as you cast it you may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1; when you\n168\t  do, copy the spell, may choose new targets).\"\n169\t- **Rulebook:** 702.153a — additional cost to sacrifice + reflexive copy trigger.\n170\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_248` (Thousand-Year Storm) — `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n171\t  + `copy_spell` + new-target choosing.\n172\t- **Seam:** `keywords = Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE`. `register_triggers`:\n173\t  on `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (now fired by **G1**) where the spell is an\n174\t  instant/sorcery controlled by `self.controller`: offer `controller.choose_yes_no`\n175\t  to pay casualty; if yes, pick a creature you control with `power >= 1` to\n176\t  `sacrifice` (engine helper), then `copy_spell(game, original_stack_obj, controller,\n177\t  new_targets)` and push the copy (mirror fdn_248's copy/new-target block).\n178\t- **New engine:** G1.\n179\t- **Edge cases:** approximation — the sacrifice is modeled as a reflexive reaction\n180\t  after the spell is on the stack (acceptable: copy resolves above original); no\n181\t  legal power≥1 creature → can't pay → no copy; only the controller's\n182\t  instants/sorceries trigger (not opponents', not Silverquill itself which is a\n183\t  creature spell); the copy is created on the stack and is itself a spell — ensure\n184\t  it does NOT recursively re-trigger casualty (guard: copies have no `colors_spent`\n185\t  / aren't \"cast\", and `copy_spell` pushes directly without going through\n186\t  `cast_spell`, so G1 won't fire for copies — verify).\n187\t\n188\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex (`GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`, Land) — mana + animation\n189\t- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}.\" / \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color, spend\n190\t  only on instant/sorcery.\" / \"{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard\n191\t  with 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.'\n192\t  Still a land.\"\n193\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (Ruby) — `get_mana_abilities` with\n194\t  `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` and the attack-style\n195\t  `ContinuousEffect`/`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` buff pattern.\n196\t- **Seam:** `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s (tap→{C}; tap+pay-1-life\n197\t  → one of any color — model the restriction by tagging the produced mana or, given\n198\t  engine limits, just add the chosen color and note the restriction can't be fully\n199\t  enforced). The {5} animation is an `ActivatedAbility` (via `get_activated_abilities`)\n200\t  whose cost pays {5} generic from the pool and whose effect, **only if CREATURE not\n201\t  in card_types**, registers PERMANENT continuous effects: `Layer.TYPE` apply →\n202\t  `self.card_types |= {CardType.CREATURE}` and add subtype \"Wizard\"; a `SET_PT`\n203\t  (7b) apply → set `self.modified_power/​modified_toughness = 2/4`. Also register a\n204\t  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (G1) for the controller's instant/sorcery casts\n205\t  that adds an end-of-turn `MODIFY_PT` `+1/+0` (Ruby's buff pattern).\n206\t- **New engine:** G1 (for the +1/+0 trigger). Animation reuses existing layer system.\n207\t- **Edge cases (highest-risk card):** `Land` is NOT a `Creature`, so:\n208\t  - the instance must define the combat attributes combat.py needs\n209\t    (`base_power`, `base_toughness`, `modified_power`, `modified_toughness`,\n210\t    `damage_marked=0`, `is_attacking=False`, `is_blocking=False`, `summoning_sick`,\n211\t    `plus_one_counters=0`, `minus_one_counters=0`) and a `power`/`toughness` read\n212\t    path. combat.py line ~228 gates attackers on `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")` — so\n213\t    consider only setting `base_power` when animated, or otherwise ensure a\n214\t    non-animated land can't be declared as an attacker.\n215\t  - `EffectManager.apply_all` resets characteristics each cycle via\n216\t    `_reset_characteristics`; override it on this card to (i) call super, (ii) reset\n217\t    `modified_power/toughness` to base, and (iii) NOT lose the animation — the\n218\t    PERMANENT TYPE effect re-adds CREATURE every cycle, so don't bake the type into\n219\t    `_original_card_types`.\n220\t  - {5} must be idempotent (\"if this land isn't a creature\"); \"still a land\" → keep\n221\t    LAND in card_types; the per-cast +1/+0 is until end of turn (DURATION_END_OF_TURN,\n222\t    swept at cleanup); summoning sickness applies to attacking but a freshly-animated\n223\t    land that's been under your control since your turn began can attack.\n224\t\n225\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (`RalZarekGuestLecturer`, Planeswalker, loyalty 3)\n226\t- **Clauses:** \"+1: Surveil 2.\" / \"−1: Any number of target players each discard a\n227\t  card.\" / \"−2: Return target creature card with mana value ≤3 from your graveyard\n228\t  to the battlefield.\" / \"−7: Flip five coins; target opponent skips their next X\n229\t  turns (X = heads).\"\n230\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito) — `get_loyalty_abilities()` returning\n231\t  `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; effects read targets off the\n232\t  source.\n233\t- **Seam:** `Planeswalker` base, `supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY}`, subtype \"Ral\".\n234\t  - **+1:** call `surveil(game, controller, 2)` (**G5**).\n235\t  - **−1:** read target players from a source attribute (set by test, e.g.\n236\t    `pw._resolve_targets`); for each, force a discard (`discard` + `choose_card`).\n237\t  - **−2:** read target creature card from `pw._resolve_target`; verify it's in your\n238\t    graveyard and `card.mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD →\n239\t    BATTLEFIELD)` under your control.\n240\t  - **−7:** flip five coins — model deterministically via `controller.choose_yes_no`\n241\t    (or `controller.choose`) five times (heads=True); `X = count(heads)`; then\n242\t    `game.skip_turns[opponent_seat] = game.skip_turns.get(opponent_seat, 0) + X`\n243\t    (**G3**).\n244\t- **New engine:** G3, G5; loyalty targets via source-attribute convention (no change).\n245\t- **Edge cases:** once-per-turn + sorcery-speed loyalty is already enforced by\n246\t  `activate_ability`; −2 must reject MV>3 or a card not in your graveyard; −1 \"any\n247\t  number\" includes zero target players; −7 with zero heads → X=0 (no skip);\n248\t  multiple skips stack (rulebook 614.10a — `skip_turns` counter accumulates);\n249\t  tests set the target attribute(s) and script the coin/discard choices before\n250\t  calling `activate_ability`.\n251\t\n252\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (`LoreholdTheHistorian`, Creature 5/5) — grants Miracle + loot\n253\t- **Clauses:** \"Flying, haste.\" / \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has\n254\t  miracle {2} (cast for miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you\n255\t  drew this turn).\" / \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard\n256\t  a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n257\t- **Analogue:** no direct FDN miracle card — closest patterns: fdn_44 emblem\n258\t  (registering a trigger that watches an event) + the `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`\n259\t  firing in `draw_card`. Loot is an upkeep trigger like fdn cards using\n260\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n261\t- **Seam:** `keywords = Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`. `register_triggers`\n262\t  registers two triggers:\n263\t  1. **Miracle** on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`: condition = `event.player is\n264\t     self.controller` AND `getattr(event.player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\", 0) == 1`\n265\t     (relies on **G4** reset) AND the drawn card's types include INSTANT/SORCERY.\n266\t     Effect: offer `controller.choose_yes_no`; if yes,\n267\t     `cast_spell_alt_cost(game, controller, card, Zone.HAND, ManaCost(generic=2))`\n268\t     (**G6**).\n269\t  2. **Loot** on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`: condition = `game.active_player\n270\t     is not self.controller` (opponent's upkeep). Effect: optional discard via\n271\t     `choose_yes_no` + `choose_card` → `discard`, then `draw_card`.\n272\t- **New engine:** G4, G6.\n273\t- **Edge cases:** miracle only on the FIRST draw of the turn (G4 reset is essential)\n274\t  and only for the controller's draws; the card is in hand when drawn — cast it from\n275\t  `Zone.HAND` paying {2}; granted-miracle applies only while Lorehold is on the\n276\t  battlefield (the trigger only exists then); loot is \"may\" (zero is legal) and the\n277\t  draw is conditional on the discard; don't offer miracle for non-instant/sorcery\n278\t  draws.\n279\t\n280\t### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares (`EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares`, Creature 3/3) — Prepared (novel)\n281\t- **Clauses:** \"When this enters, target player creates a 1/1 white-black Inkling\n282\t  with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes\n283\t  prepared. (While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so unprepares\n284\t  it.)\" Back half \"Swords to Plowshares — {W} — Instant: Exile target creature; its\n285\t  controller gains life equal to its power.\"\n286\t- **Analogue:** no FDN Prepared card. Reuse: ETB trigger + token creation\n287\t  (`create_token`) like fdn ETB cards; the activated \"cast a copy of its spell\"\n288\t  option modeled like an activated ability; STP effect (`exile` + life gain) is a\n289\t  simple targeted effect.\n290\t- **Seam:** front half is a `Creature`. `register_triggers`: ETB\n291\t  (`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, condition `event.permanent is self` /\n292\t  `event.card is self`) → target player creates an Inkling token (1/1, flying,\n293\t  white/black) via `create_token`; then set `self.prepared = True` iff an opponent\n294\t  controls more creatures than you. Expose the back-half spell as an\n295\t  `ActivatedAbility` (via `get_activated_abilities`) available only while\n296\t  `self.prepared`: cost pays {W}, effect performs Swords to Plowshares (exile target\n297\t  creature, its controller gains life = exiled creature's power) and sets\n298\t  `self.prepared = False`.\n299\t- **New engine:** none (token + exile + activated ability all exist). If\n300\t  activated-ability targeting needs a target, read it from a source attribute as the\n301\t  loyalty cards do, or via the ability's effect choosing from the battlefield.\n302\t- **Edge cases:** \"prepared\" only set when the opponent-creature-count condition\n303\t  holds at ETB; the copy is castable only while prepared and unprepares on use\n304\t  (one-shot per prepared state); Inkling token is 1/1 with flying; the target player\n305\t  for the token can be any player; if there's no legal creature to exile, the\n306\t  prepared cast should still be castable per rules but fizzle on resolve.\n307\t\n308\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone (`ImprovisationCapstone`, Sorcery — Lesson) — Paradigm (novel, hardest)\n309\t- **Clauses:** \"Exile cards from top of your library until you exile cards with\n310\t  total mana value ≥4. You may cast any number of them without paying mana costs.\"\n311\t  / \"Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n312\t  name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n313\t  beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n314\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali) for the exile-top + free-cast loop;\n315\t  fdn_244 (Progenitus) for \"go to exile instead of graveyard\"; the recurring recast\n316\t  uses **G2** + `cast_spell_free`/`copy_spell`.\n317\t- **Seam:** `Sorcery`, subtype \"Lesson\". `on_resolve`: pop top of library into exile\n318\t  until the exiled set's total `cmc >= 4`; for each exiled nonland, offer\n319\t  `choose_yes_no` then `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, card, Zone.EXILE)` (Etali loop).\n320\t  Paradigm: instead of going to the graveyard, this spell goes to exile — either\n321\t  register a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` redirect to exile (Progenitus\n322\t  pattern, destination exile) scoped to self, or move self to exile in `on_resolve`.\n323\t  Then register a recurring trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**G2**)\n324\t  for `event.player is controller` AND it's that player's FIRST main phase of the\n325\t  turn → offer to cast a copy of this card from exile for free\n326\t  (`cast_spell_free` from `Zone.EXILE`, or `copy_spell` of a fresh instance).\n327\t- **New engine:** G2 (reuses free-cast/replacement seams otherwise).\n328\t- **Edge cases:** stop exiling as soon as cumulative MV ≥ 4 (a single high-MV card\n329\t  can satisfy it); lands among exiled cards aren't castable; \"first main phases\" —\n330\t  fire only on the precombat main (the first main phase of each of the controller's\n331\t  turns), once per turn; \"after you first resolve a spell with this name\" — only set\n332\t  up the recurring effect once; the spell itself must end up in exile (not graveyard)\n333\t  for the recurring recast to find it; empty library safety.\n334\t\n335\t---\n336\t\n337\t## 3. Implementation order\n338\t\n339\tBuild the shared engine seams first (so multiple cards light up at once), then go\n340\tsimplest→hardest within each group. Run `pytest` after each card.\n341\t\n342\t1. **Engine foundation — firing + main-phase event (G1, G2, G4).** These are tiny,\n343\t   high-leverage, and unblock the most cards. G1 (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in\n344\t   `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free`) unblocks sos_226 & sos_257; G2\n345\t   (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`) unblocks sos_57 & sos_120; G4 (reset\n346\t   `cards_drawn_this_turn`) unblocks sos_201. Do them together and confirm the\n347\t   existing suite + fdn_248/fdn_44-style behavior still passes. *Rationale: one\n348\t   small batch removes the cross-cutting blockers before any card work.*\n349\t\n350\t2. **Cost-reduction / colors-spent group (reuses existing `cost_reduction` +\n351\t   `colors_spent`).** Order: **sos_4** (Converge — pure `on_resolve`, no new engine),\n352\t   then **sos_245** (self-affinity + add **G7** to grant affinity), then **sos_1**\n353\t   (cost reduction + attack free-cast + exile replacement). *Rationale: starts with\n354\t   the lowest-risk card that needs zero engine work, then layers in G7, then the\n355\t   multi-mechanic creature that combines three known patterns.*\n356\t\n357\t3. **Counter + delayed mana — sos_57** (uses **G2** from step 1; copies Refute).\n358\t   *Rationale: self-contained once G2 exists; good mid-complexity checkpoint.*\n359\t\n360\t4. **Spell-cast-trigger group (uses **G1** from step 1).** Order: **sos_226**\n361\t   (casualty copy — directly mirrors fdn_248), then **sos_257** (Great Hall —\n362\t   mana abilities are easy; the land animation via the layer system is the hard\n363\t   part and benefits from doing casualty/copy first to be comfortable with G1).\n364\t   *Rationale: shared dependency on G1; sos_257's animation is the riskiest non-novel\n365\t   card so it goes after the simpler G1 consumer.*\n366\t\n367\t5. **Planeswalker — sos_97** (adds **G3** skip-turns + **G5** surveil). *Rationale:\n368\t   four independent loyalty abilities; each ability is small but it introduces two\n369\t   new engine helpers, so isolate it.*\n370\t\n371\t6. **Novel mechanics, hardest last.** Order: **sos_201** (Lorehold — miracle via\n372\t   **G6** + loot; G4 already done), then **sos_13** (Prepared — split card + token +\n373\t   conditional state + activated copy), then **sos_120** (Paradigm — exile-until-MV\n374\t   free-cast + recurring recast from exile, the most moving parts). *Rationale:\n375\t   these have no clean FDN analogue and the most edge cases; tackle them once every\n376\t   shared seam (G1, G2, G6) and all the reusable patterns are proven.*\n377\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8998a71-cb9f-462b-a621-0c4f4edc8cf2","uuid":"4d79d2d2-8336-4e90-a051-65e84a88505f","timestamp":"2026-06-03T21:29:49.573Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN.md — SOS card implementations (1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257)\n\nThis is the hand-off from the planning phase. The implementation agent inherits\nONLY this file. Everything needed to implement the 10 cards and the supporting\nengine changes is below: exact files, hooks, events, FDN analogues, and edge\ncases. Hard rules from `AGENTS.md` still apply (additive-only engine changes —\nnever rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; class names in\n`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` must not change; write SOS tests at\n`cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, max 30 per card; do not touch `engine_tests/` or\nFDN `tests.py`).\n\nVerified engine facts this plan relies on:\n- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` pipeline pushes a `StackObject` (step 8) but\n  **never fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`** (no `fire_event` call exists in\n  casting.py). `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` is the free-cast\n  path. `cast_spell` stores `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`.\n- `engine/card.py`: hooks are `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`,\n  `on_resolve` (targets via `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets`,\n  `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`,\n  `get_modes`; `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities()`, `Land.get_mana_abilities()`.\n  `Creature.power/toughness` are computed properties; `modified_power/modified_toughness`\n  are the layer-7c write targets; `_reset_characteristics()` resets them each\n  `EffectManager.apply_all()` cycle. `ManaCost.cmc` gives mana value.\n- `engine/events.py`: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)`,\n  `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()`\n  (fires for BOTH players' upkeeps — condition must check `game.active_player`),\n  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)`, `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`\n  (has `destination`, `prevented`, `card`).\n- `engine/game.py`: `draw_card` fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` and increments\n  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` (**but this counter is never reset** — gap #4).\n  Helpers: `deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card, discard,\n  create_token, add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap`.\n- `engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` at upkeep;\n  `_do_untap_step` resets `land_plays_remaining`; **no main-phase event is fired**\n  (gap #2). `_do_cleanup_step` calls `effect_manager.remove_expired` (sweeps\n  `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`).\n- `engine/game_state.py`: `extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO popped in `advance_phase`;\n  `_normal_next_index` tracks normal rotation. **No skip-turn mechanism** (gap #3).\n- `engine/combat.py::declare_attackers_step` (line ~228) gates attacker candidates\n  on `hasattr(c, \"base_power\") and _can_attack(c)`; `_can_attack` checks\n  `summoning_sick` vs `HASTE`. Combat damage reads `getattr(creature, \"power\"/\"toughness\")`\n  and `damage_marked`. **An animated land must expose these attributes** (relevant to gap #8).\n- `engine/abilities.py`: `activate_ability` handles loyalty abilities\n  (sorcery-speed + once-per-turn enforced) but **does not plumb targets** — loyalty\n  effects read targets off the source (e.g. `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)`,\n  as fdn_44 does). Tests set the attribute before activating.\n- `engine/stack.py::copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)`\n  shallow-copies the source card, pushes a copy that resolves without zone moves.\n- `engine/continuous_effects.py`: `Layer.TYPE` (4), `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` (7)\n  with `SubLayer.SET_PT` (7b) / `MODIFY_PT` (7c); `DURATION_PERMANENT` / `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`.\n- `engine/types.py::Keyword` has FLYING, HASTE, REACH, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, etc.\n  (no AFFINITY/CONVERGE/CASUALTY/MIRACLE/SURVEIL/PREPARED/PARADIGM — those are\n  hook-driven, NOT keyword flags). `ManaType` includes COLORLESS.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Engine gaps\n\nPrefer the shared seams: firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (one change, four cards)\nand a new beginning-of-main-phase event (one change, two cards) carry most of the\nweight. Everything below is additive.\n\n| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **G1. \"Whenever you cast a spell\" triggers actually fire** | After pushing the `StackObject` in BOTH `cast_spell` (step 8) and `cast_spell_free` (step 5), call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, player=player, card=card, controller=player))`. Import the event. | `engine/casting.py` | sos_226 (casualty), sos_257 (Wizard buff); also un-breaks fdn_248/fdn_44 |\n| **G2. \"At the beginning of your next/each main phase\" trigger** | Add `@dataclass class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent): player: Any = None`. In `run_turn`, when `game.phase in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN)` and `game.step is None`, fire it with `player=game.active_player` BEFORE `priority_loop`. | `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py` | sos_57 (delayed mana), sos_120 (paradigm recast) |\n| **G3. Skip-turns** | Add `self.skip_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` to `GameState.__init__`. In `advance_phase`, after computing the would-be next `active_player_index` (from `extra_turns` or `_normal_next_index`), while `skip_turns.get(idx, 0) > 0`: decrement it, leave `_normal_next_index` pointing at that seat (so they're still \"next\" later), and set the turn to the other seat. Guard against both players skipping (infinite loop) → if all candidates are skipped, just proceed. | `engine/game_state.py` | sos_97 (−7 ultimate) |\n| **G4. Reset first-draw tracking each turn** | In `_do_untap_step`, set `game.active_player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0`. (Counter exists in `draw_card` but is never reset, so \"first card drawn this turn\" is unreliable.) | `engine/turn.py` | sos_201 (miracle) |\n| **G5. Surveil N** | New helper `surveil(game, player, n)` in `engine/game.py`: take top `n` of library; for each, ask `player.choose(\"graveyard\"/\"top\", ...)` (DeterministicPlayer scripts the answer); move chosen to graveyard via `move_to_zone`, leave rest on top. | `engine/game.py` | sos_97 (+1) |\n| **G6. Cast for an alternative cost (miracle {2})** | New helper `cast_spell_alt_cost(game, player, card, from_zone, alt_cost: ManaCost)` in `engine/casting.py`: same body as `cast_spell` but pay `alt_cost` instead of `card.mana_cost` (still run targets/`on_cast`/push/fire G1). Reuse by extracting or copying the targeting+push block. | `engine/casting.py` | sos_201 (miracle); reusable by any alt-cost card |\n| **G7. Static cost-reduction granted to OTHER spells (affinity granting)** | In `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, also add reductions contributed by the controller's permanents: `for perm in game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all(): fn = getattr(perm, \"grants_cost_reduction\", None); if callable(fn): raw += fn(game, card)`. Keep the existing `max(0, min(raw, generic))` clamp. | `engine/casting.py` | sos_245 (grants affinity to your instants/sorceries) |\n| **G8. Land becomes a creature (animation)** | No new shared engine class needed — reuse `Layer.TYPE` + `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`/`SET_PT` continuous effects. The card itself must (a) carry the creature-combat attributes combat.py reads (`base_power`, `modified_power/toughness`, `damage_marked`, `is_attacking`, `is_blocking`, `summoning_sick`, `plus_one_counters`, `minus_one_counters`) and a computed/plain `power`/`toughness`, and (b) override `_reset_characteristics` so animation re-applies each `apply_all` cycle. See sos_257 below. Only flag here: combat.py line ~228 requires `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")` for a thing to be an attacker. | `engine/continuous_effects.py` (already sufficient) | sos_257 |\n\nNote on loyalty targeting (sos_97): no engine change — follow the fdn_44\nconvention where the loyalty `effect` reads its target from an attribute on the\nplaneswalker (e.g. `pw._resolve_target` / a list you set), and tests set that\nattribute before calling `activate_ability`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Per-card plan\n\nEach card's class is already stubbed at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` extending\n`CardImpl` with `pass`; change the base class to the right type but keep the class\nname. Set `name`, `mana_cost = ManaCost.parse(...)`, types/subtypes/supertypes,\n`keywords`, and (creatures) `base_power/base_toughness` in `__init__` like the FDN\nexamples.\n\n### sos_4 — Together as One (`TogetherAsOne`, Sorcery) — Converge\n- **Clauses:** \"Converge — Target player draws X, deals X damage to any target,\n  you gain X life, where X = number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (Wardens of the Cycle) — reads colors spent.\n- **Seam:** `cast_spell` already sets `card.colors_spent` (list of `ManaType`\n  spent). In `on_resolve`, `X = len({c for c in self.colors_spent if c != ManaType.COLORLESS})`.\n  Two targets via `get_targets`: (1) target player (draw), (2) \"any target\"\n  (creature or player) for damage. Use `draw_card`, `deal_damage`, and add life.\n- **New engine:** none.\n- **Edge cases:** X=0 when only generic/colorless mana paid; target player for\n  draw may differ from damage target; damage target may be a player or creature;\n  reading `self.colors_spent` requires the spell to have been cast via `cast_spell`\n  (tests using `cast_spell` helper get this; if a test sets the board directly,\n  set `card.colors_spent` manually). Generic mana payment picks which colors are\n  spent — tests should stock the mana pool with the exact colors they want counted.\n\n### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer (`WitherbloomTheBalancer`, Creature 5/5) — Affinity (self + granted)\n- **Clauses:** \"Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control).\"\n  / \"Flying, deathtouch.\" / \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (Claws Out) — `cost_reduction` counting subtype.\n- **Seam:** Self-affinity → `cost_reduction(self, game)` returns number of\n  creatures `self.controller` controls (count battlefield objects with\n  `CardType.CREATURE`; the spell isn't on the battlefield yet so it won't count\n  itself). Keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`. Granting affinity to\n  your instants/sorceries → implement `grants_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)`\n  returning `(# creatures you control)` when `spell`'s types include INSTANT/SORCERY\n  and `spell.controller is self.controller`, else 0 — consumed by **G7**.\n- **New engine:** G7.\n- **Edge cases:** only reduces generic (engine clamps); granted reduction must NOT\n  apply to opponents' spells or to non-instants/sorceries; granted reduction stacks\n  with the spell's own `cost_reduction` (e.g. a card that also has self-affinity);\n  Witherbloom must be on the battlefield for the grant to apply (it iterates the\n  battlefield).\n\n### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic (`TheDawningArchaic`, Creature 7/7) — cost reduction + attack recast + exile replacement\n- **Clauses:** \"Costs {1} less for each instant/sorcery in your graveyard.\" /\n  \"Reach\" / \"Whenever it attacks, you may cast target instant or sorcery from your\n  graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into your\n  graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n- **Analogues:** `cards/fdn/fdn_167` (Tolarian Terror) for `cost_reduction`;\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali) for attack-trigger + `cast_spell_free`;\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_244` (Progenitus) for the graveyard→exile replacement.\n- **Seam:** `keywords = Keyword.REACH`. `cost_reduction` counts INSTANT/SORCERY in\n  `self.controller`'s graveyard (copy fdn_167). `register_triggers`: on\n  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` where `event.creature is self`, pick a target\n  instant/sorcery in your graveyard (offer via `choose_yes_no` like Etali, choose\n  the card), then **register a one-shot `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent`\n  replacement scoped to that card** (condition `event.card is the_spell`;\n  replacement moves it to exile and sets `event.prevented = True`, like Progenitus\n  but destination = exile), then `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, the_spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n- **New engine:** none (reuses existing replacement + free-cast seams).\n- **Edge cases:** no instant/sorcery in graveyard → trigger does nothing; the\n  exile-instead replacement must fire when the cast copy resolves and `_resolve_spell`\n  tries to move it to graveyard; unregister/scope the replacement so it doesn't\n  affect other cards (condition on identity); Reach is only relevant to blocking\n  (already handled by the engine's flying/reach interaction).\n\n### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt (`ManaSculpt`, Instant) — counter + delayed mana\n- **Clauses:** \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to\n  the mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) for the counter (can_cast checks stack\n  non-empty; get_targets returns stack-object target; `_counter_spell` removes from\n  `game.stack._items` and moves card to graveyard).\n- **Seam:** Copy Refute's `can_cast`/`get_targets`/`_counter_spell`. On resolve:\n  compute `mana_spent = len(target_stack_obj.source.colors_spent)` (or the spell's\n  cmc if `colors_spent` is unavailable — prefer `colors_spent` since that's the\n  literal \"mana spent\"). If `self.controller` controls a creature with subtype\n  \"Wizard\", register a **delayed trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n  (G2)** whose condition fires once for `event.player is self.controller`, adds\n  `mana_spent` `{C}` to the controller's mana pool, then self-unregisters.\n- **New engine:** G2.\n- **Edge cases:** countering fizzles if target left the stack; no Wizard → no\n  delayed mana; \"next main phase\" = the controller's next precombat OR postcombat\n  main, whichever comes first (the one-shot fires on the first matching event then\n  removes itself); record the mana amount at resolution (target is gone by then).\n\n### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant (`SilverquillTheDisputant`, Creature 4/4) — grants Casualty 1\n- **Clauses:** \"Flying, vigilance.\" / \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has\n  casualty 1 (as you cast it you may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1; when you\n  do, copy the spell, may choose new targets).\"\n- **Rulebook:** 702.153a — additional cost to sacrifice + reflexive copy trigger.\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_248` (Thousand-Year Storm) — `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n  + `copy_spell` + new-target choosing.\n- **Seam:** `keywords = Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE`. `register_triggers`:\n  on `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (now fired by **G1**) where the spell is an\n  instant/sorcery controlled by `self.controller`: offer `controller.choose_yes_no`\n  to pay casualty; if yes, pick a creature you control with `power >= 1` to\n  `sacrifice` (engine helper), then `copy_spell(game, original_stack_obj, controller,\n  new_targets)` and push the copy (mirror fdn_248's copy/new-target block).\n- **New engine:** G1.\n- **Edge cases:** approximation — the sacrifice is modeled as a reflexive reaction\n  after the spell is on the stack (acceptable: copy resolves above original); no\n  legal power≥1 creature → can't pay → no copy; only the controller's\n  instants/sorceries trigger (not opponents', not Silverquill itself which is a\n  creature spell); the copy is created on the stack and is itself a spell — ensure\n  it does NOT recursively re-trigger casualty (guard: copies have no `colors_spent`\n  / aren't \"cast\", and `copy_spell` pushes directly without going through\n  `cast_spell`, so G1 won't fire for copies — verify).\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex (`GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`, Land) — mana + animation\n- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}.\" / \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color, spend\n  only on instant/sorcery.\" / \"{5}: If not already a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard\n  with 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.'\n  Still a land.\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (Ruby) — `get_mana_abilities` with\n  `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` and the attack-style\n  `ContinuousEffect`/`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` buff pattern.\n- **Seam:** `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s (tap→{C}; tap+pay-1-life\n  → one of any color — model the restriction by tagging the produced mana or, given\n  engine limits, just add the chosen color and note the restriction can't be fully\n  enforced). The {5} animation is an `ActivatedAbility` (via `get_activated_abilities`)\n  whose cost pays {5} generic from the pool and whose effect, **only if CREATURE not\n  in card_types**, registers PERMANENT continuous effects: `Layer.TYPE` apply →\n  `self.card_types |= {CardType.CREATURE}` and add subtype \"Wizard\"; a `SET_PT`\n  (7b) apply → set `self.modified_power/​modified_toughness = 2/4`. Also register a\n  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger (G1) for the controller's instant/sorcery casts\n  that adds an end-of-turn `MODIFY_PT` `+1/+0` (Ruby's buff pattern).\n- **New engine:** G1 (for the +1/+0 trigger). Animation reuses existing layer system.\n- **Edge cases (highest-risk card):** `Land` is NOT a `Creature`, so:\n  - the instance must define the combat attributes combat.py needs\n    (`base_power`, `base_toughness`, `modified_power`, `modified_toughness`,\n    `damage_marked=0`, `is_attacking=False`, `is_blocking=False`, `summoning_sick`,\n    `plus_one_counters=0`, `minus_one_counters=0`) and a `power`/`toughness` read\n    path. combat.py line ~228 gates attackers on `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")` — so\n    consider only setting `base_power` when animated, or otherwise ensure a\n    non-animated land can't be declared as an attacker.\n  - `EffectManager.apply_all` resets characteristics each cycle via\n    `_reset_characteristics`; override it on this card to (i) call super, (ii) reset\n    `modified_power/toughness` to base, and (iii) NOT lose the animation — the\n    PERMANENT TYPE effect re-adds CREATURE every cycle, so don't bake the type into\n    `_original_card_types`.\n  - {5} must be idempotent (\"if this land isn't a creature\"); \"still a land\" → keep\n    LAND in card_types; the per-cast +1/+0 is until end of turn (DURATION_END_OF_TURN,\n    swept at cleanup); summoning sickness applies to attacking but a freshly-animated\n    land that's been under your control since your turn began can attack.\n\n### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer (`RalZarekGuestLecturer`, Planeswalker, loyalty 3)\n- **Clauses:** \"+1: Surveil 2.\" / \"−1: Any number of target players each discard a\n  card.\" / \"−2: Return target creature card with mana value ≤3 from your graveyard\n  to the battlefield.\" / \"−7: Flip five coins; target opponent skips their next X\n  turns (X = heads).\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito) — `get_loyalty_abilities()` returning\n  `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; effects read targets off the\n  source.\n- **Seam:** `Planeswalker` base, `supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY}`, subtype \"Ral\".\n  - **+1:** call `surveil(game, controller, 2)` (**G5**).\n  - **−1:** read target players from a source attribute (set by test, e.g.\n    `pw._resolve_targets`); for each, force a discard (`discard` + `choose_card`).\n  - **−2:** read target creature card from `pw._resolve_target`; verify it's in your\n    graveyard and `card.mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; `move_to_zone(... GRAVEYARD →\n    BATTLEFIELD)` under your control.\n  - **−7:** flip five coins — model deterministically via `controller.choose_yes_no`\n    (or `controller.choose`) five times (heads=True); `X = count(heads)`; then\n    `game.skip_turns[opponent_seat] = game.skip_turns.get(opponent_seat, 0) + X`\n    (**G3**).\n- **New engine:** G3, G5; loyalty targets via source-attribute convention (no change).\n- **Edge cases:** once-per-turn + sorcery-speed loyalty is already enforced by\n  `activate_ability`; −2 must reject MV>3 or a card not in your graveyard; −1 \"any\n  number\" includes zero target players; −7 with zero heads → X=0 (no skip);\n  multiple skips stack (rulebook 614.10a — `skip_turns` counter accumulates);\n  tests set the target attribute(s) and script the coin/discard choices before\n  calling `activate_ability`.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian (`LoreholdTheHistorian`, Creature 5/5) — grants Miracle + loot\n- **Clauses:** \"Flying, haste.\" / \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has\n  miracle {2} (cast for miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you\n  drew this turn).\" / \"At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard\n  a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n- **Analogue:** no direct FDN miracle card — closest patterns: fdn_44 emblem\n  (registering a trigger that watches an event) + the `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`\n  firing in `draw_card`. Loot is an upkeep trigger like fdn cards using\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n- **Seam:** `keywords = Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`. `register_triggers`\n  registers two triggers:\n  1. **Miracle** on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`: condition = `event.player is\n     self.controller` AND `getattr(event.player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\", 0) == 1`\n     (relies on **G4** reset) AND the drawn card's types include INSTANT/SORCERY.\n     Effect: offer `controller.choose_yes_no`; if yes,\n     `cast_spell_alt_cost(game, controller, card, Zone.HAND, ManaCost(generic=2))`\n     (**G6**).\n  2. **Loot** on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`: condition = `game.active_player\n     is not self.controller` (opponent's upkeep). Effect: optional discard via\n     `choose_yes_no` + `choose_card` → `discard`, then `draw_card`.\n- **New engine:** G4, G6.\n- **Edge cases:** miracle only on the FIRST draw of the turn (G4 reset is essential)\n  and only for the controller's draws; the card is in hand when drawn — cast it from\n  `Zone.HAND` paying {2}; granted-miracle applies only while Lorehold is on the\n  battlefield (the trigger only exists then); loot is \"may\" (zero is legal) and the\n  draw is conditional on the discard; don't offer miracle for non-instant/sorcery\n  draws.\n\n### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares (`EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares`, Creature 3/3) — Prepared (novel)\n- **Clauses:** \"When this enters, target player creates a 1/1 white-black Inkling\n  with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes\n  prepared. (While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so unprepares\n  it.)\" Back half \"Swords to Plowshares — {W} — Instant: Exile target creature; its\n  controller gains life equal to its power.\"\n- **Analogue:** no FDN Prepared card. Reuse: ETB trigger + token creation\n  (`create_token`) like fdn ETB cards; the activated \"cast a copy of its spell\"\n  option modeled like an activated ability; STP effect (`exile` + life gain) is a\n  simple targeted effect.\n- **Seam:** front half is a `Creature`. `register_triggers`: ETB\n  (`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, condition `event.permanent is self` /\n  `event.card is self`) → target player creates an Inkling token (1/1, flying,\n  white/black) via `create_token`; then set `self.prepared = True` iff an opponent\n  controls more creatures than you. Expose the back-half spell as an\n  `ActivatedAbility` (via `get_activated_abilities`) available only while\n  `self.prepared`: cost pays {W}, effect performs Swords to Plowshares (exile target\n  creature, its controller gains life = exiled creature's power) and sets\n  `self.prepared = False`.\n- **New engine:** none (token + exile + activated ability all exist). If\n  activated-ability targeting needs a target, read it from a source attribute as the\n  loyalty cards do, or via the ability's effect choosing from the battlefield.\n- **Edge cases:** \"prepared\" only set when the opponent-creature-count condition\n  holds at ETB; the copy is castable only while prepared and unprepares on use\n  (one-shot per prepared state); Inkling token is 1/1 with flying; the target player\n  for the token can be any player; if there's no legal creature to exile, the\n  prepared cast should still be castable per rules but fizzle on resolve.\n\n### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone (`ImprovisationCapstone`, Sorcery — Lesson) — Paradigm (novel, hardest)\n- **Clauses:** \"Exile cards from top of your library until you exile cards with\n  total mana value ≥4. You may cast any number of them without paying mana costs.\"\n  / \"Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n  name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n  beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali) for the exile-top + free-cast loop;\n  fdn_244 (Progenitus) for \"go to exile instead of graveyard\"; the recurring recast\n  uses **G2** + `cast_spell_free`/`copy_spell`.\n- **Seam:** `Sorcery`, subtype \"Lesson\". `on_resolve`: pop top of library into exile\n  until the exiled set's total `cmc >= 4`; for each exiled nonland, offer\n  `choose_yes_no` then `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, card, Zone.EXILE)` (Etali loop).\n  Paradigm: instead of going to the graveyard, this spell goes to exile — either\n  register a `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` redirect to exile (Progenitus\n  pattern, destination exile) scoped to self, or move self to exile in `on_resolve`.\n  Then register a recurring trigger on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**G2**)\n  for `event.player is controller` AND it's that player's FIRST main phase of the\n  turn → offer to cast a copy of this card from exile for free\n  (`cast_spell_free` from `Zone.EXILE`, or `copy_spell` of a fresh instance).\n- **New engine:** G2 (reuses free-cast/replacement seams otherwise).\n- **Edge cases:** stop exiling as soon as cumulative MV ≥ 4 (a single high-MV card\n  can satisfy it); lands among exiled cards aren't castable; \"first main phases\" —\n  fire only on the precombat main (the first main phase of each of the controller's\n  turns), once per turn; \"after you first resolve a spell with this name\" — only set\n  up the recurring effect once; the spell itself must end up in exile (not graveyard)\n  for the recurring recast to find it; empty library safety.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Implementation order\n\nBuild the shared engine seams first (so multiple cards light up at once), then go\nsimplest→hardest within each group. Run `pytest` after each card.\n\n1. **Engine foundation — firing + main-phase event (G1, G2, G4).** These are tiny,\n   high-leverage, and unblock the most cards. G1 (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in\n   `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free`) unblocks sos_226 & sos_257; G2\n   (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`) unblocks sos_57 & sos_120; G4 (reset\n   `cards_drawn_this_turn`) unblocks sos_201. Do them together and confirm the\n   existing suite + fdn_248/fdn_44-style behavior still passes. *Rationale: one\n   small batch removes the cross-cutting blockers before any card work.*\n\n2. **Cost-reduction / colors-spent group (reuses existing `cost_reduction` +\n   `colors_spent`).** Order: **sos_4** (Converge — pure `on_resolve`, no new engine),\n   then **sos_245** (self-affinity + add **G7** to grant affinity), then **sos_1**\n   (cost reduction + attack free-cast + exile replacement). *Rationale: starts with\n   the lowest-risk card that needs zero engine work, then layers in G7, then the\n   multi-mechanic creature that combines three known patterns.*\n\n3. **Counter + delayed mana — sos_57** (uses **G2** from step 1; copies Refute).\n   *Rationale: self-contained once G2 exists; good mid-complexity checkpoint.*\n\n4. **Spell-cast-trigger group (uses **G1** from step 1).** Order: **sos_226**\n   (casualty copy — directly mirrors fdn_248), then **sos_257** (Great Hall —\n   mana abilities are easy; the land animation via the layer system is the hard\n   part and benefits from doing casualty/copy first to be comfortable with G1).\n   *Rationale: shared dependency on G1; sos_257's animation is the riskiest non-novel\n   card so it goes after the simpler G1 consumer.*\n\n5. **Planeswalker — sos_97** (adds **G3** skip-turns + **G5** surveil). *Rationale:\n   four independent loyalty abilities; each ability is small but it introduces two\n   new engine helpers, so isolate it.*\n\n6. **Novel mechanics, hardest last.** Order: **sos_201** (Lorehold — miracle via\n   **G6** + loot; G4 already done), then **sos_13** (Prepared — split card + token +\n   conditional state + activated copy), then **sos_120** (Paradigm — exile-until-MV\n   free-cast + recurring recast from exile, the most moving parts). *Rationale:\n   these have no clean FDN analogue and the most edge cases; tackle them once every\n   shared seam (G1, G2, G6) and all the reusable patterns are proven.*\n","numLines":377,"startLine":1,"totalLines":377}}}
