{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory has a `card_spec.json` (oracle text/metadata) and a `card_impl.py` stub. Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples. Follow inherited `/workspace/PLAN.md` (engine-gap specs G1–G8, FDN analogues, per-card plans).\n\n   Methodology constraints (MUST continue to apply, verbatim intent):\n   - Strict TDD using the `tdd` skill: write a failing test through the engine's public interface (test_utils), watch it fail (red), write minimal code (green). The established working pattern this session: write the full per-card test file → run to confirm red → implement → run green.\n   - Test the real engine, drive cards as a player would through test_utils.\n   - Reuse before you add; mirror the nearest FDN card; keep engine edits minimal/shared.\n   - **Guard the engine: after each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a regression (baseline 1145 passing).**\n   - **Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/`. Do NOT modify or add FDN `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`.**\n   - **Additive-only engine modifications**: may add methods/classes/helpers/files in engine/ and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Card class names in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` must not change. SOS tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, max 30 per card.\n   - The FINAL user message: respond TEXT ONLY (this summary), no tool calls.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Miracle (alt cost on first draw), loot, Prepared (novel), Swords to Plowshares, Paradigm (novel — exile-until-MV + recurring free recast from exile), Inkling token, planeswalker loyalty, surveil, skip-turns, casualty, affinity, converge, counter+delayed mana, land animation, coin flips, reanimation.\n   - Engine hooks: `on_resolve(game)` (reads `self.chosen_targets`), `register_triggers(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()` (returns `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`), `get_loyalty_abilities()`, `get_mana_abilities()`, `can_cast(game)`, `get_targets(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)`, `grants_cost_reduction(game, card)`, `_reset_characteristics()`.\n   - **Self-ETB limitation (critical)**: `zones.py::move_to_zone` lines 301-317 fire `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` BEFORE calling `card.register_triggers(game)` (the docstring at lines 207-210 says the opposite and is WRONG). So a permanent's own ETB self-trigger registered in `register_triggers` does NOT catch its own entry. Solution (fdn_2 precedent): handle self-ETB in `on_resolve`. Note `_resolve_spell` calls `card.on_resolve(game)` BEFORE moving the permanent to battlefield, so in on_resolve the card is NOT yet on the battlefield (account with +1 for self when counting \"creatures you control\").\n   - Trigger system: `TriggerManager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller))`. `condition(game, event)->bool`, `effect(game)->None`. `fire_event(game, event)` only PUSHES matching StackObjects (APNAP order), does NOT auto-resolve; resolution needs `_resolve_top_of_stack`. Condition runs at fire time; stashing data on source in the condition (e.g. `source._miracle_card = card`) is the established pattern (sos_226 `_casualty_spell`).\n   - Events (field names): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)`; `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_precombat)` (fired in turn.py for precombat True and postcombat False); `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (no fields — fired for BOTH players; condition must check `game.active_player`); `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)` (game.py increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` BEFORE firing, reset to 0 in turn.py `_do_untap_step`); `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller, card, creature)`.\n   - Casting: `cast_spell(game, player, card)` (timing+can_cast+hand+targets+pay+on_cast+push+fire G1); `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (no mana/timing); NEW `cast_spell_alt_cost(game, player, card, from_zone, alt_cost)` (skip timing, source from_zone, pay alt_cost, fire G1). `_resolve_spell` moves permanents→battlefield, instant/sorcery→graveyard, OR→exile if `getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolution\", False)` (the Paradigm redirect hook).\n   - `ManaCost(generic=0, pips={}, x_count=0, hybrid=[])` — all defaulted; `ManaCost.parse(str)`; `ManaCost.cmc` = mana value (X=0). Lands typically have no mana_cost → MV 0.\n   - Abilities runtime: `activate_ability(game, player, instance)`. `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability)`; `cost(game, source)->bool` (return False → AbilityError \"cost could not be paid\"); non-mana abilities push StackObject(on_resolve=effect). `AbilityError` importable from engine.abilities. Loyalty abilities: sorcery-speed + once-per-turn.\n   - test_utils: `create_game()`, `set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)` (NOT library; sets owner/controller), `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` (sets sorcery-speed for non-instants, calls engine cast, then `_resolve_top_of_stack`), `_resolve_top_of_stack(game)` (pop+on_resolve+SBA until stack empty). DeterministicPlayer pops choices FIFO from `_script` (choose_yes_no/choose/choose_card/choose_target). Triggers are NOT auto-registered by set_board_state — tests call `card.register_triggers(game)` manually after placing on battlefield (sos_226 pattern).\n   - ZoneContainer: index -1 = top; `get_all()[-1]` = top of library. `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone)`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` (MODIFIED — added G6):\n     - Added `cast_spell_alt_cost` between `cast_spell_free` and `_resolve_spell`. Body: skip timing; `if not card.can_cast(game): raise CastingError`; locate card in `player.zones[from_zone]`; move to stack zone; clear `colors_spent`; set controller/owner; choose targets with filter_fn + protection (rollback to source on failure); `if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(alt_cost): rollback + raise`; `player.mana_pool.pay(alt_cost)`; `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`; `card.on_cast(game)`; push StackObject with `_on_resolve` → `_resolve_spell`; fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, player=player, card=card, controller=player)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` (CREATED, DONE — 14 tests pass):\n     - `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`. __init__: name \"Lorehold, the Historian\", mana_cost {3}{R}{W}, subtypes {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, supertypes {LEGENDARY}, keywords FLYING|HASTE, base_power/toughness 5.\n     - `register_triggers`: helper `_is_instant_or_sorcery(obj)` checks INSTANT/SORCERY in card_types. Miracle trigger on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`: condition = `event.player is source.controller` AND `getattr(event.player,'cards_drawn_this_turn',0)==1` AND drawn card is instant/sorcery (stashes `source._miracle_card`); effect = read `_miracle_card`, set to None, check in hand, `ctrl.choose_yes_no`, then `cast_spell_alt_cost(game, ctrl, card, Zone.HAND, ManaCost(generic=2))` wrapped in try/except CastingError. Loot trigger on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`: condition = `ctrl is not None and game.active_player is not ctrl`; effect = if hand non-empty and `ctrl.choose_yes_no`, `ctrl.choose_card`, `discard`, `draw_card`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (CREATED, 14 tests, all pass): `_GainLife(Sorcery)` ({4}{R}, +3 life on resolve), `_creature`, `_set_library` (bottom-to-top). Classes: TestProperties(6), TestMiracle(5: first_instant_draw_cast_for_two, decline_keeps_card, non_first_draw, noncreature_required, only_controller_draws), TestLoot(3: on_opponent_upkeep, declined_no_draw, no_loot_on_own_upkeep). Loot tests set `game.active_player_index = 1` and use creature library cards to avoid miracle interference.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` (CREATED, DONE — 13 tests pass):\n     - Module helpers: `_make_inkling()` → `Creature(name=\"Inkling\", base_power=1, base_toughness=1, subtypes={\"Inkling\"}, keywords=Keyword.FLYING)` with `token.colors = {\"W\",\"B\"}`; `_count_creatures(game, player)` counts CREATURE card_types on battlefield.\n     - `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`. __init__: name \"Emeritus of Truce\" (front-face name chosen, not full split name), mana_cost {1}{W}{W}, subtypes {\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}, base_power/toughness 3; `self.prepared = False`.\n     - `on_resolve` (handles self-ETB because engine fires ETB before register_triggers): create Inkling for `getattr(self,\"_token_target\",None) or ctrl`; `mine = _count_creatures(ctrl) + 1`; `opp_max = max((_count_creatures(p) for p in players if p is not ctrl), default=0)`; `if opp_max > mine: self.prepared = True`.\n     - `get_activated_abilities` returns one `ActivatedAbility`: `_stp_cost` returns False if not prepared else pays {W}; `_stp_effect` sets `source.prepared=False` first, reads `source._resolve_target`, checks CREATURE, reads power BEFORE exile, `exile(game, target)`, `tgt_controller.life += power`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (CREATED, 13 tests, all pass): helpers `_creature`, `_cast_emeritus(game, token_target=None)` (sets `em._token_target`, casts), `_inklings`, `_activate_stp`. Classes: TestProperties(5), TestEnterToken(3), TestPrepared(2), TestSwordsToPlowshares(3: exiles_and_grants_life, requires_prepared via pytest.raises(AbilityError), cannot_activate_twice).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` (CREATED — JUST WRITTEN, NOT YET TESTED):\n     - `_mana_value(card)` returns `card